1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,303
25,000 rats and not a single disease,

2
00:00:03,303 --> 00:00:05,662
What's the secret of Deshnoke?

3
00:00:05,662 --> 00:00:10,381
In a small town in Rajasthan, there is a unique temple.

4
00:00:10,381 --> 00:00:14,628
Here, rats are not chased away, they are fed.

5
00:00:14,628 --> 00:00:18,403
People don't see them as pests, they see them as their ancestors.

6
00:00:18,403 --> 00:00:22,650
And this is exactly what amazes the whole world.

7
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:28,592
This is the Karni Mata temple, in Deshnoke, near Bikaner.

8
00:00:28,592 --> 00:00:33,995
A white marble floor, and black rats running across it.

9
00:00:33,995 --> 00:00:38,316
Devotees walk barefoot, very carefully.

10
00:00:38,316 --> 00:00:42,098
You have to look down at every step.

11
00:00:42,098 --> 00:00:47,500
Because here, the real guests of the floor are not humans, but rats.

12
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,501
But the real question is this. So many rats, so much crowd,

13
00:00:51,501 --> 00:00:55,502
then why is there no fear of disease? The devotees say,

14
00:00:55,502 --> 00:00:59,059
this is the Mother's blessing. Doctors say,

15
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:02,171
rats carry dangerous germs.

16
00:01:02,171 --> 00:01:06,616
Today we will examine all of this with evidence, no joking,

17
00:01:06,616 --> 00:01:07,950
without passing judgment.

18
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:13,405
The story is from many centuries ago, from the burning deserts of Rajasthan.

19
00:01:13,405 --> 00:01:18,859
There was a holy woman there, whom people call Karni Mata.

20
00:01:18,859 --> 00:01:22,826
The Charan community, an old community of Rajasthan,

21
00:01:22,826 --> 00:01:28,281
has deep faith in her. For them it is not just a story,

22
00:01:28,281 --> 00:01:30,760
it is a memory of their own home.

23
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:34,552
Now imagine, a mud-plastered courtyard, evening time.

24
00:01:34,552 --> 00:01:39,766
A grandmother sits surrounded by children. She says,

25
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:44,032
once a great sorrow came upon the Mother's family.

26
00:01:44,032 --> 00:01:49,246
The Mother did not give up. She went straight to Yamraj,

27
00:01:49,246 --> 00:01:52,090
the god of death.

28
00:01:52,090 --> 00:01:55,601
According to the story, a deal was made there.

29
00:01:55,601 --> 00:02:01,118
The people of the Mother's family would not wander anywhere after death.

30
00:02:01,118 --> 00:02:05,632
They would become rats and stay near the Mother.

31
00:02:05,632 --> 00:02:11,149
In this very temple, in this very courtyard. The grandmother smiles and says,

32
00:02:11,149 --> 00:02:14,660
that's why the rats here are our own.

33
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:19,990
These rats are called kaba here. Kaba means sacred rats,

34
00:02:19,990 --> 00:02:25,320
whom people consider their ancestors. Ancestors means our forefathers,

35
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:30,651
who lived before us. Just think, what the world calls a rat,

36
00:02:30,651 --> 00:02:34,043
could be someone's great-grandfather.

37
00:02:34,043 --> 00:02:36,950
That's why nobody here kills them.

38
00:02:36,950 --> 00:02:40,533
Now let me make one thing clear, honestly.

39
00:02:40,533 --> 00:02:43,668
This story doesn't come from any written scripture,

40
00:02:43,668 --> 00:02:47,699
it comes from local tradition. It is passed down, generation after generation,

41
00:02:47,699 --> 00:02:52,626
It's been passed down by word of mouth. That's why this panel is labeled legend.

42
00:02:52,626 --> 00:02:54,417
That doesn't mean it's a lie,

43
00:02:54,417 --> 00:02:58,000
only that we don't have written proof.

44
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,306
Now let's move from the story to the stone.

45
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:05,347
The temple you see today is not very old.

46
00:03:05,347 --> 00:03:06,816
According to Rajasthan Tourism,

47
00:03:06,816 --> 00:03:10,122
its construction was completed in the early part of the last century.

48
00:03:10,122 --> 00:03:14,530
The work was done under the supervision of Maharaja Ganga Singh of Bikaner.

49
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:19,751
The whole temple is made of marble, from top to bottom.

50
00:03:19,751 --> 00:03:22,883
Its design has the Rajput style,

51
00:03:22,883 --> 00:03:28,627
and a touch of the Mughal style too. Style means the way of building,

52
00:03:28,627 --> 00:03:33,847
like arches, lattice screens and carvings. The craft of different eras,

53
00:03:33,847 --> 00:03:36,980
visible on a single wall.

54
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:41,829
As soon as you enter the temple, your eyes get stuck on the doors.

55
00:03:41,829 --> 00:03:44,738
These are doors of solid silver.

56
00:03:44,738 --> 00:03:48,132
Their panels have raised carvings.

57
00:03:48,132 --> 00:03:53,466
Raised carving means a picture that stands out from the surface.

58
00:03:53,466 --> 00:03:57,830
These pictures are carved with the stories of Karni Mata.

59
00:03:57,830 --> 00:04:01,272
That is, the story that grandmother tells by word of mouth

60
00:04:01,272 --> 00:04:06,190
is written on the silver too. Just not in words,

61
00:04:06,190 --> 00:04:07,174
but in pictures.

62
00:04:07,174 --> 00:04:12,092
Many devotees stop in front of the door and bow their heads.

63
00:04:12,092 --> 00:04:16,026
Some people look at every panel carefully,

64
00:04:16,026 --> 00:04:19,960
as if they are turning the pages of a book.

65
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:25,304
Inside is the sanctum, the innermost holy room of the temple.

66
00:04:25,304 --> 00:04:29,190
There is a stone idol of Karni Mata there.

67
00:04:29,190 --> 00:04:34,049
According to Rajasthan Tourism, its height is about 0.75 meters.

68
00:04:34,049 --> 00:04:39,393
That means about as tall as a small child. The idol holds a trident in its hand,

69
00:04:39,393 --> 00:04:40,850
and a crown on its head.

70
00:04:40,850 --> 00:04:45,280
Around the idol there are also statues of her sisters.

71
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:50,153
The idol is decorated with a crown and garlands, and in front is a line of devotees.

72
00:04:50,153 --> 00:04:54,584
And right here, near the sanctum, rats also gather.

73
00:04:54,584 --> 00:04:59,900
It looks as if they too are standing in the line for darshan.

74
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:04,075
Now look up. A mesh screen is fitted over the courtyard,

75
00:05:04,075 --> 00:05:05,466
for protection.

76
00:05:05,466 --> 00:05:11,033
This mesh protects the rats from danger coming from above,

77
00:05:11,033 --> 00:05:16,135
like predatory birds. That means the temple doesn't just tolerate the rats.

78
00:05:16,135 --> 00:05:20,310
It also makes complete arrangements for their protection.

79
00:05:20,310 --> 00:05:24,047
Now, about the temple's biggest secret.

80
00:05:24,047 --> 00:05:26,383
Among thousands of black rats,

81
00:05:26,383 --> 00:05:31,522
Sometimes a white rat appears. And when it does,

82
00:05:31,522 --> 00:05:36,661
a stir spreads through the courtyard. People point,

83
00:05:36,661 --> 00:05:41,800
and whisper. Everyone's eyes settle on the same corner.

84
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:42,227
Why?

85
00:05:42,227 --> 00:05:46,919
Because white rats are considered especially sacred.

86
00:05:46,919 --> 00:05:48,626
Rajasthan Tourism writes,

87
00:05:48,626 --> 00:05:53,318
that people believe they are the avatars of Karni Mata and her sons.

88
00:05:53,318 --> 00:05:58,011
An avatar means the form a god or goddess takes on earth.

89
00:05:58,011 --> 00:06:01,850
That's why seeing a white rat is considered great good fortune.

90
00:06:01,850 --> 00:06:06,708
Devotees work very hard to call them out.

91
00:06:06,708 --> 00:06:10,595
They lay out sweets and wait quietly for hours.

92
00:06:10,595 --> 00:06:16,424
A mother holds her son's hand and peeks into the corner.

93
00:06:16,424 --> 00:06:18,853
Just one glimpse, that's all.

94
00:06:18,853 --> 00:06:22,740
For them, this is a direct blessing from the Mother.

95
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:28,442
Now guess, how many rats are there here? According to one estimate,

96
00:06:28,442 --> 00:06:34,145
about 25,000 black rats. Among them, the white ones can be counted on your fingers.

97
00:06:34,145 --> 00:06:36,219
So finding a white rat

98
00:06:36,219 --> 00:06:40,366
is like looking for one special face in a crowd.

99
00:06:40,366 --> 00:06:45,550
This rarity is what makes it even more sacred.

100
00:06:45,550 --> 00:06:48,208
One point about science too.

101
00:06:48,208 --> 00:06:51,930
The black rats here are Rattus rattus.

102
00:06:51,930 --> 00:06:54,588
That is, the same common black rat

103
00:06:54,588 --> 00:06:58,310
that is found in homes and warehouses.

104
00:06:58,310 --> 00:07:03,627
It's not some unusual species. The difference is only in how people see it.

105
00:07:03,627 --> 00:07:07,880
Outside, they are considered enemies; here, family.

106
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:09,321
Now the question

107
00:07:09,321 --> 00:07:13,643
that you are probably watching this video for.

108
00:07:13,643 --> 00:07:17,004
Is it really true that disease doesn't spread here?

109
00:07:17,004 --> 00:07:21,326
The devotees' claim is very big. They say,

110
00:07:21,326 --> 00:07:26,128
this place has stayed untouched by plague. Plague is the epidemic

111
00:07:26,128 --> 00:07:29,490
that spreads through rat fleas.

112
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:32,292
Now hear an even more shocking claim.

113
00:07:32,292 --> 00:07:35,093
The prasad that the rats have tasted

114
00:07:35,093 --> 00:07:38,695
is considered very sacred. Devotees say,

115
00:07:38,695 --> 00:07:41,497
eating it does no harm.

116
00:07:41,497 --> 00:07:45,098
This claim is tied to the faith of many people.

117
00:07:45,098 --> 00:07:47,900
We are not taking it lightly.

118
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:52,467
Now listen to the other side. Medical researchers say,

119
00:07:52,467 --> 00:07:55,665
rats carry dangerous pathogens.

120
00:07:55,665 --> 00:07:59,775
Pathogens means those tiny germs that spread disease.

121
00:07:59,775 --> 00:08:04,343
This applies to rats all over the world.

122
00:08:04,343 --> 00:08:08,910
The rats of Deshnoke are also, biologically, the same Rattus rattus.

123
00:08:08,910 --> 00:08:11,835
So what is the truth? Listen plainly.

124
00:08:11,835 --> 00:08:15,597
There is no verified study to back this claim.

125
00:08:15,597 --> 00:08:19,776
It has not been proven that disease never happens here.

126
00:08:19,776 --> 00:08:23,955
Nor has it been proven that disease spreads more here.

127
00:08:23,955 --> 00:08:26,880
There are claims, but no measured data.

128
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:30,735
One difference is important to understand here. No disease happening,

129
00:08:30,735 --> 00:08:35,018
and no record of disease, are two different things.

130
00:08:35,018 --> 00:08:40,157
Sometimes we take a lack of records as proof itself.

131
00:08:40,157 --> 00:08:43,155
But an empty register proves nothing.

132
00:08:43,155 --> 00:08:47,010
It only tells you that nobody counted.

133
00:08:47,010 --> 00:08:51,838
Researchers point to one thing that is missing: an epidemiological study,

134
00:08:51,838 --> 00:08:56,184
that is, a large-scale account of people's health.

135
00:08:56,184 --> 00:09:01,012
How many people came, how many fell ill, and why.

136
00:09:01,012 --> 00:09:05,357
No such systematic study has been done at this temple.

137
00:09:05,357 --> 00:09:09,220
So science cannot give a verdict yet.

138
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,907
That is why this panel carries the label "disputed".

139
00:09:11,907 --> 00:09:15,362
It means devotees and experts say different things.

140
00:09:15,362 --> 00:09:17,665
Devotees speak of faith.

141
00:09:17,665 --> 00:09:19,968
Doctors speak of caution.

142
00:09:19,968 --> 00:09:22,655
And in between is that empty space,

143
00:09:22,655 --> 00:09:26,110
where proof should have been, but isn't yet.

144
00:09:26,110 --> 00:09:27,819
If you go there,

145
00:09:27,819 --> 00:09:31,236
take the doctors' caution along with you.

146
00:09:31,236 --> 00:09:35,081
Wash your hands well, be careful if you have a cut,

147
00:09:35,081 --> 00:09:39,352
keep an eye on the children. This is not against faith.

148
00:09:39,352 --> 00:09:44,051
It is simply responsibility for your own health. Seeing the Mata,

149
00:09:44,051 --> 00:09:45,760
and looking after yourself too.

150
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:49,820
Now, the things that nobody knows even today. First of all,

151
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:53,511
how fast do these rats die? Their death rate,

152
00:09:53,511 --> 00:09:56,095
that is, how many rats die every year,

153
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:58,310
has never been properly measured.

154
00:09:58,310 --> 00:10:02,370
Nobody has these numbers for such a big colony.

155
00:10:02,370 --> 00:10:07,786
Then comes the question of parasites. Parasites, like fleas and insects,

156
00:10:07,786 --> 00:10:10,740
that live off another creature.

157
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:15,170
The same thing can increase the risk of disease,

158
00:10:15,170 --> 00:10:20,586
or reduce it. But how many parasites these rats carry,

159
00:10:20,586 --> 00:10:23,540
there is no measured record of that.

160
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:26,580
And the most interesting question is this.

161
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:30,632
Why don't the rats leave the temple and go outside?

162
00:10:30,632 --> 00:10:34,685
Around it is a desert town, open and big.

163
00:10:34,685 --> 00:10:39,244
Still, the colony mostly stays inside the temple.

164
00:10:39,244 --> 00:10:42,790
Devotees call this Mata's bond.

165
00:10:42,790 --> 00:10:45,830
Science only has guesses.

166
00:10:45,830 --> 00:10:49,357
One guess is a full meal every day.

167
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:53,388
Sweets and prasad, everything is available right here,

168
00:10:53,388 --> 00:10:58,427
so why go outside? Another guess is social habituation.

169
00:10:58,427 --> 00:11:03,969
That means the animals get used to one place and to people.

170
00:11:03,969 --> 00:11:08,000
But these are all guesses, not yet proven.

171
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:14,131
So you see, the story has an answer, science has questions.

172
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:20,262
And this is what makes this place so special. A temple

173
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:24,721
where faith and science stand face to face.

174
00:11:24,721 --> 00:11:28,066
And in between, thousands of rats, unaware,

175
00:11:28,066 --> 00:11:31,410
eating prasad in comfort.

176
00:11:31,410 --> 00:11:34,067
If you want to visit Deshnoke,

177
00:11:34,067 --> 00:11:36,724
it is near Bikaner.

178
00:11:36,724 --> 00:11:41,595
Information about this temple is available on the Rajasthan Tourism website.

179
00:11:41,595 --> 00:11:44,695
When you arrive, first look at the silver doors.

180
00:11:44,695 --> 00:11:48,237
Every panel is a story. If you stop and look,

181
00:11:48,237 --> 00:11:51,780
you will understand the whole tale through the pictures.

182
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:56,874
Inside is a marble courtyard, with a protective mesh above.

183
00:11:56,874 --> 00:12:02,533
In the sanctum is a statue about 0.75 metres tall, with a trident.

184
00:12:02,533 --> 00:12:08,759
And rats are everywhere on the floor. You have to walk barefoot,

185
00:12:08,759 --> 00:12:14,418
so walk slowly. Don't hurt anyone, neither yourself,

186
00:12:14,418 --> 00:12:15,550
nor them.

187
00:12:15,550 --> 00:12:19,897
Remember, this is not a museum, it is a living temple.

188
00:12:19,897 --> 00:12:24,727
People come here to worship and to make wishes.

189
00:12:24,727 --> 00:12:29,558
Take photos, but don't make fun of anyone's faith.

190
00:12:29,558 --> 00:12:34,388
Whatever you came to see, look at it with your heart. Ask questions,

191
00:12:34,388 --> 00:12:36,320
but with respect.

192
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:39,050
And yes, keep your eyes out for the white rat.

193
00:12:39,050 --> 00:12:43,340
Maybe you won't see it even after hours. Maybe you'll see it as soon as you arrive.

194
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:47,240
The hope in the eyes of the people standing there

195
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:49,970
is a sight in itself.

196
00:12:49,970 --> 00:12:53,090
That moment doesn't fit completely in any photo.

197
00:12:53,090 --> 00:12:56,550
So what is the conclusion for today?

198
00:12:56,550 --> 00:13:01,309
The temple's marble and silver are in the Rajasthan Tourism records.

199
00:13:01,309 --> 00:13:05,634
The story of the rats is in local tradition. The disease claim

200
00:13:05,634 --> 00:13:10,392
is so far without any study. These are all different things,

201
00:13:10,392 --> 00:13:13,420
And they should be looked at in a different way.

202
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:18,198
In the next journey, we will head toward the sea. A city,

203
00:13:18,198 --> 00:13:23,411
which is said to have sunk into the water.

204
00:13:23,411 --> 00:13:26,886
Its name is Dwarka. What was found there, who found it,

205
00:13:26,886 --> 00:13:30,795
and whether there are still questions, all with proof.

206
00:13:30,795 --> 00:13:34,270
Until then, remember this story of Deshnoke.

207
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:37,726
Now, one simple question for you.

208
00:13:37,726 --> 00:13:42,909
If a white rat comes in front of you in Deshnoke,

209
00:13:42,909 --> 00:13:46,365
what will you do? Will you take a photo,

210
00:13:46,365 --> 00:13:52,700
or fold your hands and quietly stop? Do tell us in the comments.
